# Allen Relation: DURING / CONTAINS
#
# DURING: interval A occurs entirely within interval B.
#   A during B  iff  B.start < A.start and A.end < B.end
#
# CONTAINS: the symmetric inverse — B fully encloses A.
#   B contains A  iff  B.start < A.start and A.end < B.end
#
# Legal patterns that trigger DURING / CONTAINS:
#   "during the term of this agreement"
#   "within the period of validity"
#   "consultations shall begin within X days" (consultation during agreement)
#   "for the duration of the contract"
#   any obligation or procedure that must occur within a larger validity window
#
# Grounded example (en_contracts_seed0, Article 9.3):
#   Consultation period [request_date, result_deadline] is DURING
#   agreement active period [signature_date, 2006-12-31].
#   The agreement CONTAINS the consultation interval.

```catala
declaration scope AllenDuring:
  input outer_start content date   # start of the containing period
  input outer_end content date     # end of the containing period
  input inner_start content date   # start of the contained period
  input inner_end content date     # end of the contained period
  output is_during content boolean    # inner occurs entirely within outer
  output is_contains content boolean  # outer fully encloses inner
```

## DURING

The inner interval starts after the outer starts and ends before the
outer ends — it is fully contained.

```catala
scope AllenDuring:
  date round down
  definition is_during equals
    (outer_start < inner_start) and
    (inner_end < outer_end)
```

## CONTAINS

The symmetric statement from the outer interval's perspective.

```catala
scope AllenDuring:
  definition is_contains equals
    (inner_start > outer_start) and
    (outer_end > inner_end)
```
